{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the man shall bring his wife.</b> It is not said 'afterwards' — for in any case where his wife has strayed from the ways of modesty and breached his trust, and he sits and broods over it, this is nothing but ill will of heart. And even though it is hidden from his eyes that a man lay with her, we are not concerned to invalidate his jealousy. And likewise if he was jealous without cause, it is not for this reason said that his jealousy should be a void thing — for even so the scroll is blotted out and he brings [the offering] as written in the pericope."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:42.956522474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}